## 5. Proposed backend-neutral contract

### 5.1 Design boundary

Use two related values:

1. SceneChangeSet is a logical, backend-neutral description of a scene transition. It contains stable IDs and serializable immutable data, never Vulkan, D3D12, Metal, native descriptor, pointer, or RHI handle values.
2. ApplySceneChangeRequest binds that logical transition to one renderer instance, device generation, mapping snapshot, and active-scene epoch. This prevents backend/device data from contaminating the editor contract while still fencing application.

The same canonical SceneChangeSet can therefore be tested on CPU, applied to Vulkan or D3D12, rejected as unsupported on Metal, and queued while Android presentation is suspended.

### 5.2 Illustrative C++ shape

The following is a contract sketch, not a mandate on exact naming:

~~~cpp
struct StableSceneId {
  EditorObjectKind kind;
  DocumentAuthority authority;
  uint32_t slot;
  uint32_t generation;

  auto operator<=>(const StableSceneId&) const = default;
};

enum class SceneChangeDomain : uint8_t {
  DocumentMutation,
  SceneActivation,
  FullSnapshot
};

struct SceneChangeHeader {
  uint32_t schemaVersion;
  SceneChangeDomain domain;
  DocumentAuthority authority;
  uint64_t baseDocumentRevision;
  uint64_t targetDocumentRevision;
  uint64_t baseSceneEpoch;
  uint64_t targetSceneEpoch;
  StableSceneId activeSceneId;
  MutationToken mutationToken;
  uint64_t mutationSerial;
  ProjectionDigest baseProjectionDigest;
  ProjectionDigest targetProjectionDigest;
  ChangeSetDigest canonicalChangeSetId;
};

struct ImmutableBufferPayload {
  ContentHash contentHash;
  BufferSemantic semantic;
  uint64_t logicalOffset;
  uint64_t byteSize;
  SharedImmutableBytes bytes;
};

struct ImmutableTexturePayload {
  ContentHash contentHash;
  TextureSchema schema; // dimensions, format, mip/layer count, color space
  vector<TextureSubresourcePayload> subresources;
};

using SceneOperation = variant<
    SetNodeTransform,
    SetNodeLocalVisibility,
    SetMaterialProperties,
    SetMaterialTextureBinding,
    SetPrimitiveMaterialBinding,
    SetVariantSelection,
    SetCameraProperties,
    SetCameraAttachment,
    SetLightProperties,
    SetLightAttachment,
