## 17. Acceptance criteria for P5 readiness

P5 renderer-delta readiness requires all of the following:

- Exact typed editor changes; no use of the current all-live changedIds as a precise delta.
- Stable-ID-keyed canonical SceneChangeSet with deterministic serialization/digest.
- Authority, revision, projection digest, mapping epoch, scene epoch, renderer instance, device instance, and device-generation fences.
- Stale generation rejection before any renderer/RHI side effect.
- Immutable, atomically published stable-ID-to-actual-runtime-handle mapping.
- Deterministic coalescing and dependency ordering with CPU tests under shuffled input.
- Incremental transform, visibility, material/binding/variant, camera, and light paths.
- Explicit, transactional full snapshot for scene switch, global Merge, Compact, and unsupported topology cases.
- Geometry and texture upload contracts with exact byte/subresource counters, correct barriers/states, and submission-aware retirement.
- Explicit apply status and complete pre-submit/post-submit rollback behavior.
